From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:31:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Skip impossible qualified-card legacy alias scans

Why: links-source projection indexed receipts by origin, but still scanned that
bucket for every qualified card. supersedes rejects a non-None profile before
reading any receipt. A captured source composition performed 296,941 such
immediately rejected comparisons for 6,335 legacy-list cards.

Move only that exact first rejection ahead of the scan. Keep the origin-key
lookup before it to preserve malformed/unhashable-origin failure ordering.
Keep by-key and compression-tip suppression for every card. No memberships,
clocks, active streams or terminal deadlines are cached or skipped.

Proof:
- Behavioral RED on parent c99417f4aa: 4 failed, 9 passed; failures assert work.
- Expanded focused regression: 16 passed; 95 passed across the initial three
  focused files before adding three falsey-profile controls.
- Direct-importer suite: 163 files, 2,965 tests passed, zero failures.
- Three exact-anchor mutants killed: omitted gate, truthiness gate, skipped
  qualified origin lookup. Full scripts/check: 21 checks passed.
- Twenty alternating captured parent/candidate source-composition pairs have
  exact ordered cards and ledger-slice parity (5,842 cards). Median thread CPU
  290.230 -> 258.615 ms on a loaded worker, all raw samples retained.
  This is diagnostic: plain SQLite opener, unavailable local authority/empty
  local dedup, omitted cold durable carry and frozen clock. It is NOT live
  links-family acceptance; the prior mature Mac pair still fails at 0.8053%.

Task: t_eeeeee0000000018. Read-only Mac capture; no signal/restart/update.
